 "title": "CI: delete the kept build once it passes 30 GB",
 "body": "CARGO_TARGET_DIR under `~/.cache/illogical-ci` is kept between runs and cargo never prunes it. On 2026-10-02 it reached 136 GB on jake-mini, filled the disk and took the home cluster's master VM (and Forgejo) down; geek was at 134 GB too.\n\nEach job now runs `scripts/ci-cap-target 30` first, which deletes the kept build once it passes 30 GB. It runs at job start, so it never touches a build in progress. The home-cloud side adds a 40 GB host-level backstop and disk alerts (home-cloud#43).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
